==Strategy==
Due to its shield blocking status effects, you must either use brute force to destroy Aku Cyclone or use [[:Category:Shield Piercing Cats|Shield Piercers]], such as [[Lilin (Uber Rare Cat)|Lilin]] or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs]]. Regardless, the main strategy is to use stackable DPS units such as [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and gradually whittle it down.

For stalling, [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] are your best choice. If you happen to have unlocked [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]] and her target Aku Talent, she can work as well, since the stage features exclusively Red and Aku enemies. [[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]] is also good to have, as it can dodge attacks from Aku enemies and is disposable, though it might struggle if the nasty Ginger Snaches get in the way.

A good [[Cat Combo|Combo]] to use is [[Little Warriors (Combo)|Little Warriors]]. It gives you Cameraman and [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Lil' Eraser Cat]] to work with along with a highly accessible Unit Defense UP for your other meatshields. Add another small Defense Combo, such as [[Sportswoman (Combo)|Sportswoman]], and you should have your meatshielding game good to go. If you didn't use a Shield Piercer to beat this stage, well then enjoy your reward!

